<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — MorphoEval overall 54.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py` (weighted score: 54.6/100). The Pass 1 script integrates only a single-cell two-face PIN1 carrier competition ODE at p=1.0 and p=2.0 without a 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice, without comparing Feugier Model A conserved open dendritic trees (Betti-1 = 0) against Model B saturating Hill exocytosis + Scarpella (2006) epidermal convergence closed reticulate loops (Betti-1 > 0) and bipolar bridge cells, without a `gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis ablation negative control, and without empirical CV segmentation of the vendored cleared leaf tip venation skeleton specimen. Overall 54.1/100 (faithfulness 51.6, reproducibility 59.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 56, Morphological realism / specimen match 46, Parameter expressivity 52, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 58, Reproducibility package 54. Output judged: docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py at 8871db0, image/png, 53533 B, 1200×504 px, artifact_sha256 2d5b0781a005c1b7c878d9f96f9ac6cd6599e509cdfd967fe1f5303bf1ee9108 (sha256 2d5b0781a005c1b7c878d9f96f9ac6cd6599e509cdfd967fe1f5303bf1ee9108), spec_fingerprint 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c; artifact_sha256: 2d5b0781a005c1b7c878d9f96f9ac6cd6599e509cdfd967fe1f5303bf1ee9108; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/carrier_driven_canalization_reference.json=d1b984c1cb7883c5..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg=e54c8add6cf7c916..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/paper_citations.bib=cb81009f386f3a51..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/scout_manifest.json=1de2b4f4c53ac234...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a `gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis ablation negative control (k_1 = 0) demonstrating complete loss of membrane PIN1 polarization and vascular strand formation.",
        "remediation needed: Compare Feugier Model A conserved power-law allocation Phi(J) = max(0,J)^p (winner-take-all single-face polarization, open dendritic venation trees with Betti-1 = 0) against Model B saturating Hill allocation Phi(J) = J^n/(K^n + J^n) and Scarpella et al. (2006) epidermal PIN1 convergence points (stabilizing bipolar PIN1 bridge cells and closed reticulate venation loops with Betti-1 > 0).",
        "remediation needed: Implement a 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice solver (6 faces per cell) integrating Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) intracellular auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_{ij} and pairwise antisymmetric flux J_{i->j} + J_{j->i} = 0.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the SHA-256-verified cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`) to extract vein density, closed polygonal areole loop count (Betti-1 = 205), mean areole area, and mean areole compactness, and expose a comprehensive 8-check `--self-test` suite." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.41e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

